      "text": "To find the product of the base seven numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) and then determine the base seven sum of the digits of this product, we follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base seven numbers to base ten.\n2. Multiply the base ten equivalents.\n3. Convert the product back to base seven.\n4. Find the sum of the digits of the base seven product.\n\n**Step 1: Convert \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base ten.**\n\nThe base seven number \\(24_7\\) can be converted to base ten as follows:\n\\[\n24_7 = 2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}\n\\]\n\nThe base seven number \\(30_7\\) can be converted to base ten as follows:\n\\[\n30_7 = 3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21_{10}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Multiply the base ten equivalents.**\n\nNow, we multiply the base ten equivalents:\n\\[\n18_{10} \\times 21_{10} = 378_{10}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Convert the product \\(378_{10}\\) back to base seven.**\n\nTo convert \\(378_{10}\\) to base seven, we repeatedly divide by 7 and keep track of the remainders:\n\\[\n378 \\div 7 = 54 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n54 \\div 7 = 7 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 5\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\div 7 = 1 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\div 7 = 0 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1\n\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get:\n\\[\n378_{10} = 1050_7\n\\]\n\n**Step 4: Find the sum of the digits of the base seven product.**\n\nThe base seven number \\(1050_7\\) has digits 1, 0, 5, and 0. The sum of these digits is:\n\\[\n1 + 0 + 5 + 0 = 6\n\\]\n\nThus, the base seven sum of the digits of the product is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
